issuecomment-2844124470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103657","id":2844124470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pheU2","user":{"login":"RobProductions","id":11141862,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTQxODYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11141862?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions","html_url":"https://github.com/RobProductions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T05:16:01Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T05:16:01Z","body":"@HeadZerg That's basically what https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/93431 accomplishes, so no need to make that change in this PR (though there are minor differences, the detection method for out of date files is similar, so whichever PR gets merged first could potentially introduce reusable functionality for the other). There is some concern in that discussion that there could be C# assembly changes not just from files changing but from external dependencies as well, and in the case of the user absolutely needing an up to date assembly when hitting the play button, that check matters.\r\n\r\nHowever, looking at just this PR, since compilation always happens when you press play anyways, there's no need to worry about that for this branch. The 