criptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-10T06:52:00Z","updated_at":"2026-07-10T06:52:00Z","body":"Tested this on 4.8-dev, if the build fails for any reason it continuously attempts to re-build over and over again regardless of success. This occurs with Automatic Build set to On Focus and Always.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure how you would handle this case, as On Focus loops due to the editor constantly regaining focus when you click \"okay\" on the failure pop-up. Maybe some sort of flag that prevents further automatic building if the last build was a failure? Though I guess the real solution is to not write code that doesn't compile :upside_down_face: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4932766713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5071211639","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103657#issuecomment-5071211639","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103657","id":5071211639,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLkSMdw","user":{"login":"RobProductions","id":11141862,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTQxODYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11141862?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions","html_url":"https://github.com/RobProductions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-24T14:54:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T14:54:42Z","body":"> Maybe some sort of flag that prevents further automatic building if the last build was a failure? \r\n\r\nThanks for checking it out! This is probably the best solution and should be simple enough to add to the PR (if we have access to build success state somewhere), I just don't have time anymore to look into it especially after waiting over a year for a review since my schedule has changed drastically. If you want to pull down the branch and supersede it with a fix that's totally cool with me, or if you have a direct code change that I can merge in to this PR I can give it a shot as well. \r\n\r\nIf there is actual traction on the PR and I find the time, I could try taking a look as well. I would like to see this improvement added, I've just lost nearly all hope for it after linking it in the contributor chat every single time we exited feature freeze since it went up .-.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5071211639/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5073306248","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103657#issuecomment-5073306248","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103657","id":5073306248,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLmSCiA","user":{"login":"Komariarii","id":301026105,"node_id":"U_kgDOEfFLOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301026105?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii","html_url":"https://github.com/Komariarii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-24T18:43:44Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T18:43:44Z","body":"> I've just lost nearly all hope for it after linking it in the contributor chat every single time we exited feature freeze since it went up .-.\r\n\r\nSuch is the way of the night before godot-dotnet I suppose...\r\n\r\nWriting a fix for it should be relatively simple, though I have a UI improvement in mind, in my asynchronous branch I added a progress bar to the backing of the build button, I think it'd be maybe a neat idea if the backing changed colors as well? Such as orange for out of date and red for the last build failing? Otherwise once you close the \"Failed to Build\" prompt there's nothing in the editor explicitly telling you that's the case. \r\nThough maybe the out of date state should be reserved for the PR that lets you skip building if the assembly is up to date. \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5073306248/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5447612722","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103657#issuecomment-5447612722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103657","id":5447612722,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRLP5Mg","user":{"login":"Komariarii","id":301026105,"node_id":"U_kgDOEfFLOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301026105?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii","html_url":"https://github.com/Komariarii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T02:23:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T02:28:38Z","body":"\r\n[fixBadBuildLoop.patch](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31537695/fixBadBuildLoop.patch)\r\nHere's a quick (only a month later...) patch to prevent the infinite loop soft-lock that occurs when you get a failed build. This changes BuildProject to return a bool which I think somewhat makes sense. \r\n\r\nThis currently has a UX issue of not being very clear that automatic builds are temporarily disabled, we could put that into the \"build failed\" pop-up if the user has auto building turned on, but I would like to personally see something like this:\r\n\"Warning\" colored border to indicate a build is required\r\n<img width=\"342\" height=\"52\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bdb6cc4c-7df0-4d7e-8119-e63ea1c19e89\" />\r\n\r\nand a \"Error\" (or well redish in this case because I dont have the exact color) for the last build being a failure\r\n<img width=\"310\" height=\"41\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4552bec3-61cc-4640-b287-bedd8dc9031d\" />\r\n\r\nThis would fit (I think) nicely with the asynchronous PR which has the middle of the button turn into indeterminate progress bar, letting you get a pretty decent \"at-a-glimpse\" look at the status of the assembly. This'll cause a merge conflict, but I'd happily fix it for whichever PR gets merged first. \r\n\r\nYou also mentioned making a potentially superseding PR, but I think I still fall underneath new contributor status, and this is technically a feature...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5447612722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5922744833","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103657#issuecomment-5922744833","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103657","id":5922744833,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYQXqAQ","user":{"login":"RobProductions","id":11141862,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTQxODYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11141862?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions","html_url":"https://github.com/RobProductions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobProductions/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T01:16:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T01:16:10Z","body":"> [fixBadBuildLoop.patch](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31537695/fixBadBuildLoop.patch) Here's a quick (only a month later...) patch to prevent the infinite loop soft-lock that occurs when you get a failed build. This changes BuildProject to return a bool which I think somewhat makes sense.\r\n\r\nThis is awesome, thanks so much for the contribution! I'm sorry for leaving this unresolved for so long, been busy clawing back some time in my schedule and when I do have time, I try to put it directly into actually making my game instead of getting stuck in PRs forever haha. But things are stabilizing a tiny bit recently so maybe in a few weeks or months I could be able to look into this.\r\n\r\nWhen I do find the time I will merge in your patch and add you as a co-author to the commit, hopefully that's allowed within the new contributor rules since I've reviewed it. Apologies again for being absent, but at a glance resolving the conflict and applying the fix shouldn't be too bad. I'll be sure to comment here when I've made progress :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5922744833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5924875656","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103657#issuecomment-5924875656","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103657","id":5924875656,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYSZtiA","user":{"login":"Komariarii","id":301026105,"node_id":"U_kgDOEfFLOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301026105?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii","html_url":"https://github.com/Komariarii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T04:41:02Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T04:41:11Z","body":"I believe I meet the criteria now? Though I don't know how \"big\" those 3 merged commits have to be. \r\n\r\nUnfortunately there seems to be something with automatic building causing a crash, at least when in combination with my asynchronous PR, I frankly kind of find it hard to use Godot without asynchronous C# building now so I haven't organically tested it by itself. \r\nMy guess is that it's somehow causing multiple builds to stack ontop of each other, resulting in the crash (though of course this is just a hunch), I'll likely need to find some time to set aside to see if I can get it to happen without async building... \r\n\r\nI was thinking of maybe making another PR that implements some FileWatcher based hooks so that PRs like this one and \"compile on change\" can use that, enabling the ability to skip a build on focus if the assembly is already up to date.\r\nThough I have no knowledge of FileWatchers at the moment so I'm not sure how I'd implement it quite yet, would be nice though! \r\n\r\nIt seems like the mono module has been given some renewed focus in lieu of godot-dotnet, so there's some hope for these long outstanding PRs such as yours to get in now I believe.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5924875656/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5930309416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103657#issuecomment-5930309416","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103657","id":5930309416,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYXlXKA","user":{"login":"Luceid71","id":99190798,"node_id":"U_kgDOBemIDg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99190798?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71","html_url":"https://github.com/Luceid71","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luceid71/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T11:23:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T11:23:39Z","body":"Perhaps this is a bit late in the game, but I just wanted to ask. Wouldn't it be a lot simpler and easier just to add an option to skip automatic rebuild? I imagine a lot of the people who want this feature have IDEs that auto build for them after saving code changes. I custom build my godot to just strip the auto build out. Having an option would basically fix this for most people, without the need for error prone checks on godot's side.\r\n\r\nI understand that this would be a different PR, but it feels like a simple boolean in options would pass through Godot's highly congested PR ecosystem much easier. And it would fix the issue for a lot of people.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5930309416/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5930578250","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103657#issuecomment-5930578250","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103657","id":5930578250,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYX1xSg","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T11:41:57Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T11:41:57Z","body":"@Luceid71 You can see the PR and the reasons not to here https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120709 (if anything it is harder to pass it)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5930578250/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5938439697","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103657#issuecomment-5938439697","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103657","id":5938439697,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYfVmEQ","user":{"login":"Komariarii","id":301026105,"node_id":"U_kgDOEfFLOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301026105?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii","html_url":"https://github.com/Komariarii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T18:58:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T18:58:41Z","body":"@Luceid71  Skipping the build on play is part of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/93431, ideally these two PRs (automatic build on focus and compile only on change) will work together to make it a smoother process. \r\nIE: you program in your IDE/code editor, you alt tab back into Godot, the C# project automatically starts building and pressing play will immediately get you into the game, creating a flow nearly as seamless as GDScript is. \r\n\r\nI agree that a flag in the editor settings would be kind of a foot gun, as it's incredibly easy to forget about and the only thing warning you in the editor that your project is outdated is the properties of a node, but only if that node has a script that's directly affected by changes. \r\n\r\nWhile the process for these PRs may be slow, I think the usability factor should be the priority, which is roughly what these PRs accomplish. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5938439697/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]